From: arch-port <26345330+DrShadow34@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:11:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] panvk: frame shaders load cube attachments as 2D arrays

The preload shaders (pan_fb_nir.c) sample cube views (layered rendering
into a cube or cube array) as 2D arrays, but the texture descriptor kept
the cube dimension: layer N then addressed cube N and every layer past
the first loaded out of bounds. CTS geometry.layered.cube*.readback /
secondary_cmd_buffer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013fD3if93WntovhmD8fGa8C
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c
index 6219e7a..12d3bdf 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c
@@ -357,6 +357,11 @@ fill_textures(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
       }
 
       struct pan_image_view pview = *iview;
+      /* the frame shaders load cube views (layered rendering) as 2D arrays
+       * (pan_fb_nir.c), the descriptor has to match: as a cube one, layer N
+       * would be cube N */
+      if (pview.dim == MALI_TEXTURE_DIMENSION_CUBE)
+         pview.dim = MALI_TEXTURE_DIMENSION_2D;
       if (loc == FRAG_RESULT_DEPTH)
          pview.format = util_format_get_depth_only(pview.format);
       else if (loc == FRAG_RESULT_STENCIL)
